Fillets: the cut of a blend's end by a face at the end that the blend
meets in a loop through both its points is the way round inside the face
(mitcad#1425).

The case of 1580: the bar's blend run on past the chain's end crosses the
tip's rounding of 4 (a cylinder) from its edge with the tip's side to its
edge with the corner patch. The blend's surface and the cylinder, each
bounded by PerformIntersectionAtEnd's box about the two points, meet in a
loop through both, and ChFi3d_ComputeCurves took the way round it outside
the cylinder's face, past the corner patch's edge: the cylinder's face
was grown over the blend's face (area 73.7 against the file's 55.2 mm2),
0.27 mm off the stored body.

- PerformIntersectionAtEnd: where the curve computed on a face at the end
  that is not prolonged has its middle outside the face, it is computed
  again on the surface bounded by the face's own domain (one hundredth of
  it wider), and taken where its middle lies inside the face.

On the design's stored body before the item: the cylinder's face as the
file's (its cut within 0.0007 mm of the file's).

